invariant: INV-7
file: suite.h
catches: webpki_session_aes
reason: a host object's session whose caller did not set
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES takes the AES-first default order whenever any
  bit is set, so its client offers AES-256-GCM and AES-128-GCM and its
  server selects one of them, and the traffic keys then run AES
  instructions whose timing nobody stated. test_webpki_runtime_answers
  requires the hello under the probe's bit alone to list ChaCha20 alone.

--- old
    if ((cfg->cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES) == 0) {
--- new
    if (cfg->cpu == 0) {
